/T (Modern authoritarian leaders rarely rely only on violence. Instead, they use information, technology, and emotion to stay in control. The spread of the internet has given them new tools for propaganda. Social media can be used to monitor citizens, spread false news, or create confusion about what is true and what is not. Many regimes also try to control education and culture, shaping how people think from a young age. The goal is not simply to make people obey, but to make them believe that obedience is natural and necessary.)
